{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence","id":1216255,"title":"Question on Quintessence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-07T12:13:30-07:00","id":1216255,"title":"Question on Quintessence","content":"I am playing an RPG for the first time, and the ST has made a hot mess involving Mage: The Ascension (2nd edition I believe), Werewolf: The Reckoning, and something about Changelings. W/e, my Virtual Adept doesn't believe in fairies.<br /> <br /> I am trying to understand how to use Prime. Is there a way to create Tass, or is it only obtained from Nodes? And for the rote in Prime called &quot;The Rush&quot;, it mentions that you can store additional Quintessence internally, beyond your avatar rating. It says you can roll once per source of quintessence to store it internally, but seems to say that you are getting this from whatever is flowing free through your own pattern, which indicates to me that there can only ever be the one source. Is this a rote that can only be used once, or can it be used to store quintessence from an external source, like a Node or passing cat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24175-sodellar","name":"Sodellar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T12:28:15-07:00","id":1216257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sodellar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence#post1216255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am playing an RPG for the first time, and the ST has made a hot mess involving Mage: The Ascension (2nd edition I believe), Werewolf: The Reckoning, and something about Changelings. W/e, my Virtual Adept doesn't believe in fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhhh. Best...make sure that's what's being used, as Mage 2nd edition is ancient, Werewolf: The Reckoning could be Hunter: The Reckoning or Werewolf: The Apocalypse...<br /> But, okay! Let's keep things strictly Mage here, and mostly edition-agnostic.<br /> <br /> First off, yes, you can use Prime to store more Quintessence inside your Mage than what the Avatar rating normally allows. The advantage is, of course - moar Quintessence! The disadvantage is that to others able to sense Prime, it can get more obvious, the more you store. Still, it tends to be a thing that is handy to do - even if just a little bit.<br /> <br /> As for the sources thing - that is, sadly, not Edition agnostic. if I recall, Mage 20th makes no mention of there only being one source per roll, while 2nd (and I think Revised) do.<br /> But no, there can be more than one source - you can simply only use one roll (per scene/downtime) per source: &quot;The mage may make only one roll per source of Quintessence&quot;<br /> <br /> ..and yeah, you're definitely using Mage 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> The reference about free flowing Quintessence inside your pattern is fluff - as it states, normally life patterns like a Mage's body do not hold extra Quintessence. Instead they constantly pull Quintessence from external sources - nourishment, air, etc. and also constantly lose it - burning nourishment, waste, and such. That's essentially the metaphysics of life patterns in mage.<br /> But Prime 2 allows you to store extra Quintessence inside your body - with said rote. That's what the extra points of Quintessence are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-07-2018, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T12:56:23-07:00","id":1216272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence?p=1216257#post1216257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhhh. Best...make sure that's what's being used, as Mage 2nd edition is ancient, Werewolf: The Reckoning could be Hunter: The Reckoning or Werewolf: The Apocalypse...<br /> But, okay! Let's keep things strictly Mage here, and mostly edition-agnostic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Apocalypse. He is getting ready to dump a Hunter into our game.<br /> <br /> So, are you saying that it would basically be saving a little extra quintessence while eating a good meal, or hyperventilating, once a scene? Drawing more out of what the character normally does?<br /> <br /> And is there a way to make Tass, or is that only a game creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24175-sodellar","user":"Sodellar","date":". 05-07-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24175-sodellar","name":"Sodellar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:00:59-07:00","id":1216295,"title":"","content":"Ah, no. The sources of Quintessence that you can tap with that level of Prime are not just everyday objects. Sorry if the explanation of how Life Patterns work made you confused in that regard.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 can get used to draw Quintessence from Nodes, Tass and Periapts. The latter get into the realm of Wonders and wonder creation, so let's ignore those for now;<br /> Nodes produce free Quintessence and Tass every week, and Prime 2 can be used to draw it from them, past the limit that your Avatar rating allows; Normally, mere meditation at a node is enough to fill up to that Avatar rating limit.<br /> <br /> Also, as I mentioned above, Tass gets created at Nodes, but I do recall there being ways to actually make it - or rather, turn everday things into Tass - by using Prime again to infuse something with Quintessence. I'd have to look up any references though, I'm not sure which book mentioned it. Don't take my word for it right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:19:47-07:00","id":1216304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence?p=1216295#post1216295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as I mentioned above, Tass gets created at Nodes, but I do recall there being ways to actually make it - or rather, turn everday things into Tass - by using Prime again to infuse something with Quintessence. I'd have to look up any references though, I'm not sure which book mentioned it. Don't take my word for it right now.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you. I remember seeing something at level two called Fuel Pattern that didn't seem to have much of a description, but that seems kinda low for that kind of storage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24175-sodellar","name":"Sodellar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:44:27-07:00","id":1216572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence?p=1216295#post1216295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, no. The sources of Quintessence that you can tap with that level of Prime are not just everyday objects. Sorry if the explanation of how Life Patterns work made you confused in that regard.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 can get used to draw Quintessence from Nodes, Tass and Periapts. The latter get into the realm of Wonders and wonder creation, so let's ignore those for now;<br /> Nodes produce free Quintessence and Tass every week, and Prime 2 can be used to draw it from them, past the limit that your Avatar rating allows; Normally, mere meditation at a node is enough to fill up to that Avatar rating limit.<br /> <br /> Also, as I mentioned above, Tass gets created at Nodes, but I do recall there being ways to actually make it - or rather, turn everday things into Tass - by using Prime again to infuse something with Quintessence. I'd have to look up any references though, I'm not sure which book mentioned it. Don't take my word for it right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't you absorb Quintessence from a Node with Prime 1?<br /> <br /> Also, any Mage can absorb Quintessence from a Node, slowly, by Meditating (or equivalent). However this only replenishes their stores up to their Avatar rating, and never any higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T05:46:49-07:00","id":1216586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence?p=1216572#post1216572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you absorb Quintessence from a Node with Prime 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup! Sorry for that. Prime 1 is enough. I habitually tend to start any non-perceptions-only effects at 2 reflexively, but Mind and Prime both break that mold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, any Mage can absorb Quintessence from a Node, slowly, by Meditating (or equivalent). However this only replenishes their stores up to their Avatar rating, and never any higher </div> </div> </div>Yes. As the words that you quoted say, 'Normally, mere meditation at a node is enough to fill up to that Avatar rating limit.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T05:52:11-07:00","id":1216588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence?p=1216586#post1216586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup! Sorry for that. Prime 1 is enough. I habitually tend to start any non-perceptions-only effects at 2 reflexively, but Mind and Prime both break that mold.<br /> <br /> Yes. As the words that you quoted say, 'Normally, mere meditation at a node is enough to fill up to that Avatar rating limit.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I missed that. Apologies.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is weird that Mind and Prime have mechanical impacts outside of perception (and the related advantages). But I can see why it is the case with Mind; you are enhancing your perception of thoughts and emotions, and that buffing your Perception, Wits and Intelligence makes a great deal of sense. Even so, I could understand if someone house-ruled those effects into Mind 2. As for Prime... not really sure why Prime 1 lets you absorb more Quintessence (that does feel like Level 2, you're right).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:08:23-07:00","id":1216596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216255-question-on-quintessence?p=1216588#post1216588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah I missed that. Apologies.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is weird that Mind and Prime have mechanical impacts outside of perception (and the related advantages). But I can see why it is the case with Mind; you are enhancing your perception of thoughts and emotions, and that buffing your Perception, Wits and Intelligence makes a great deal of sense. Even so, I could understand if someone house-ruled those effects into Mind 2. As for Prime... not really sure why Prime 1 lets you absorb more Quintessence (that does feel like Level 2, you're right).</div> </div> </div> </div>Every sphere has their unique quirks that make them deviate from the \u201cstandard\u201d sphere rules.<br /> <br /> Prime is an interesting one. I usually see it as Prime magic requiring quintessence for almost all of their effects, so the first thing you need to learn is how to hold it.<br /> <br /> Keeping it in line with sensory, you could say holding extra quintessence is a result of an enhanced capability to be aware of quintessence, and thus retain more than your avatar can within its power. While arguably other mages who can\u2019t sense quintessence don\u2019t really hold quintessence at all, but instead it\u2019s their avatar that does the holding.<br /> <br /> As for Mind, the first Mind you learn to sense of your own, but you also control your own mind intrinsically, so the added awareness of how your mind operates allows for an even greater level of control.<br /> With this extra insight, you can directly shift around certain aspects of how your mind operates. Emphasising attention and focus, allowing for an increase in cognitive abilities and memory recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-08-2018, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}